{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"a74b565ccbbdc7a5","name":"card_unit_p_40_k","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Legions/units/card_unit_p_40_k","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"P-40 K","text":"When a friendly bomber is destroyed, destroy a random enemy unit.","flavorText":"The Curtiss P-40 Warhawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft that was first introduced in 1938 and used during WWII by many Allied air forces. Due to a limited supply of Merlin engines that had powered previous Warhawks, the P-40K variant had it replaced with a new and more powerful Allison engine that had an automated boost control. The first 600 P-40k variants were produced in 1942 and shipped to China under Lend-Lease. The idea was to produce it in limited numbers as this would be the last P-40 series, the plan was to replace it with the P-60. However, problems with production of the P-60 meant that the production was increased to a total of 1,300 P-40k’s, including a few sub variants. Most P-40k’s served with the US air forces in Asia and the Pacific and with the Chinese Air Forces, but a few were sent to Britain under Lend-Lease and were redesignated as Kittyhawk III.","faction":"USA","type":"fighter","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_p_40_k","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p_40_k_title","SourceString":"P-40 K","LocalizedString":"P-40 K"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p_40_k_text","SourceString":"When a friendly bomber is destroyed, destroy a random enemy unit.","LocalizedString":"When a friendly bomber is destroyed, destroy a random enemy unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p_40_k_history","SourceString":"The Curtiss P-40 Warhawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft that was first introduced in 1938 and used during WWII by many Allied air forces. Due to a limited supply of Merlin engines that had powered previous Warhawks, the P-40K variant had it replaced with a new and more powerful Allison engine that had an automated boost control. The first 600 P-40k variants were produced in 1942 and shipped to China under Lend-Lease. The idea was to produce it in limited numbers as this would be the last P-40 series, the plan was to replace it with the P-60. However, problems with production of the P-60 meant that the production was increased to a total of 1,300 P-40k’s, including a few sub variants. Most P-40k’s served with the US air forces in Asia and the Pacific and with the Chinese Air Forces, but a few were sent to Britain under Lend-Lease and were redesignated as Kittyhawk III.","LocalizedString":"The Curtiss P-40 Warhawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft that was first introduced in 1938 and used during WWII by many Allied air forces. Due to a limited supply of Merlin engines that had powered previous Warhawks, the P-40K variant had it replaced with a new and more powerful Allison engine that had an automated boost control. The first 600 P-40k variants were produced in 1942 and shipped to China under Lend-Lease. The idea was to produce it in limited numbers as this would be the last P-40 series, the plan was to replace it with the P-60. However, problems with production of the P-60 meant that the production was increased to a total of 1,300 P-40k’s, including a few sub variants. Most P-40k’s served with the US air forces in Asia and the Pacific and with the Chinese Air Forces, but a few were sent to Britain under Lend-Lease and were redesignated as Kittyhawk III."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes